<ref name="ReviewsRoundup">Summaries of critical reception attributed to the following references:
* {{Cite web |last=Campbell |first=Christopher |date=February 28, 2022 |title=''The Batman'' First Reviews: Not Just a Good Batman Movie, but One of the Best Comic Book Movies Ever |url=https://editorial.rottentomatoes.com/article/the-batman-first-reviews/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220301000408/https://editorial.rottentomatoes.com/article/the-batman-first-reviews/ |archive-date=March 1, 2022 |access-date=August 12, 2025 |publisher=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] |quote=Critics say Matt Reeves' gritty, grounded take on the 'World's Greatest Detective' is one of the best we've seen, from Robert Pattinson's performance down to the cinematography and the score.}}
* {{Cite magazine |last=Sharf |first=Zack |date=February 28, 2022 |title=''The Batman'' Review Roundup: An 'Exhilarating', 'Unforgettable' and 'Overlong' Comic Book Film |url=https://variety.com/2022/film/news/the-batman-review-roundup-critics-1235191908/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220228182330/https://variety.com/2022/film/news/the-batman-review-roundup-critics-1235191908/ |archive-date=February 28, 2022 |access-date=August 12, 2025 |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |quote=One thing critics agree on when it comes to ''The Batman'' is that there has never been a comic book movie like it before. [...] The review embargo for Matt Reeves' ''The Batman'' has lifted, bringing with it a handful of raves and several mixed takes on the director's very long and very dark interpretation of the Caped Crusader.}}
* {{Cite web |last=Weiss |first=Josh |date=February 28, 2022 |title=One of the best superhero movies ever? ''The Batman'' reviews hail Matt Reeves reboot as 'perfection' |url=https://www.syfy.com/syfy-wire/the-batman-matt-reeves-robert-pattinson-reviews |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220228184342/https://www.syfy.com/syfy-wire/the-batman-matt-reeves-robert-pattinson-reviews |archive-date=February 28, 2022 |access-date=August 12, 2025 |website=[[Syfy Wire]] |quote=''Syfy Wire'' has seen the film and is happy to report that ''The Batman'' is not only great, but also makes the central hero feel fresh again after so many revivals and continuities. Other critics agree with us and some are going so far as to call this one of the greatest — if not the greatest — superhero movie ever made. And with all due respect to the Nolan trilogy, it might just be the best Batman title ever made.}}
* {{Cite web |last=Whitten |first=Sarah |date=March 3, 2022 |title=''The Batman'' is a refreshing adaptation, but 'handcuffed' by its PG-13 rating, critics say |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2022/03/02/the-batman-reviews-what-critics-thought-of-the-new-dark-knight-film.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220303013821/https://www.cnbc.com/2022/03/02/the-batman-reviews-what-critics-thought-of-the-new-dark-knight-film.html |archive-date=March 3, 2022 |access-date=August 12, 2025 |publisher=[[CNBC]] |quote=The film, which arrives in theaters on Friday, has elicited mixed reactions from critics. Some have praised the nearly three hour-long feature as a deconstruction of the superhero genre, others found it to be a dark slog.}}</ref>

<ref name="ReviewsRoundup2">Further summaries of critical reception attributed to the following references:
* {{Cite web |last=Bonomolo |first=Cameron |date=February 28, 2022 |title=''The Batman'' Reviews and Reactions Round-Up: What Critics Are Saying |url=https://comicbook.com/movies/news/the-batman-movie-reviews-reactions-roundup-what-critics-are-saying/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220228183031/https://comicbook.com/movies/news/the-batman-movie-reviews-reactions-roundup-what-critics-are-saying/ |archive-date=February 28, 2022 |access-date=August 12, 2025 |website=[[ComicBook.com]] |quote=Early reviews compare ''The Batman'' to Christopher Nolan's 2005 franchise-reviving reboot ''Batman Begins'', similarly set in the early years of Bruce Wayne's (Christian Bale) costumed crime-fighting career. [...] Other reviews criticize a 'weak' final act.}}
* {{Cite web |last=Venable |first=Heidi |date=February 28, 2022 |title=''The Batman'' Reviews Have Dropped, Here's What Critics Are Saying About Robert Pattinson's Caped Crusader |url=https://www.cinemablend.com/superheroes/batman/the-batman-reviews-have-dropped-heres-what-critics-are-saying-about-robert-pattinsons-caped-crusader |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220228173747/https://www.cinemablend.com/superheroes/batman/the-batman-reviews-have-dropped-heres-what-critics-are-saying-about-robert-pattinsons-caped-crusader |archive-date=February 28, 2022 |access-date=August 12, 2025 |website=[[CinemaBlend]] |quote=Several critics make note of this version's serious tone and Robert Pattinson as what Leah Greenblatt of ''EW'' calls possibly 'the Darkest Knight yet'. [...] But he's not the only critic who takes issue with the film's finale, saying it betrays the rest of the movie's vision. [...] The critics also all make note of the detective story that highlights ''The Batman''.}}
* {{Cite news |last=Parkel |first=Inga |date=March 3, 2022 |title=''The Batman'' reviews: Critics praise Robert Pattinson and Zoë Kravitz performances in new Matt Reeves blockbuster |url=https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/films/news/the-batman-2022-reviews-release-robert-pattinson-b2027977.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250601074000/https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/films/news/the-batman-2022-reviews-release-robert-pattinson-b2027977.html |archive-date=June 1, 2025 |access-date=August 12, 2025 |newspaper=[[The Independent]] |quote=''The Batman'' is receiving positive reviews from critics ahead of its release, with Robert Pattinson and Zoe Kravitz's performances singled out for praise. [...] While critics seem hesitant to give too much credit to Matt Reeves' new film, so far it seems that the new movie is being considered a worthy addition to the canon. [...] Many critics also grumbled about the three-hour-long run time.}}
* {{Cite web |last=Gonzalez |first=Umberto |date=February 28, 2022 |title=First ''The Batman'' Reviews Hail Robert Pattinson Reboot as 'Best Bat-Movie Yet' |url=https://www.thewrap.com/the-batman-reviews-reactions-roundup/ |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220228184833/https://www.thewrap.com/the-batman-reviews-reactions-roundup/ |archive-date=February 28, 2022 |access-date=August 12, 2025 |website=[[TheWrap]] |quote=Critics all agree that ''The Batman'' ranks among the best Batman movies, if not the best Batman film as Matt Reeves delivers a grounded take of the Dark Knight detective in a film noir that has shades of ''Seven'', ''Zodiac'' and ''Chinatown'' thrown in for good measure. [...] Reviews also note that Pattinson, who stars as the Dark Knight detective, gets to be the active protagonist in his film, instead of being a supporting character to a villain that chews up the scenery like previous films. [...] Others note that ''The Batman'' might be the best Batman movie yet.}}</ref>

